homelab-notes (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The note's "..." menu (pin, share, move, history, copy link, delete)
    opens from a real click: the click bubbled to the document-level
    handlers that close any open menu, so it closed in the same instant
    it opened and delete was unreachable (post-cutover #71 reopened,
    found by Gardner). The trigger now stops propagation like the notebook
    and folder menus do; the live check opens the menu for real and
    deletes and restores a note through it.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:30:00 -0600

homelab-notes (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Links between notes (post-cutover #93): [[Note title]] and [[Title|shown
    as]] in a Markdown or wiki body link to the note with that title (the
    same notebook first, then what the viewer may see); a title with no note
    shows as missing and, for someone who may edit, a tap makes that note.
    On a share link's page a link resolves only inside the shared notebook.
  * A fourth format, wiki (MediaWiki markup), rendered by the package's own
    Homelab::Notes::Wikitext through the same cleaner: headings, bold and
    italic, * and # lists, definition lists, rules, [[links]], [url text],
    tables, preformatted lines, <pre> and <nowiki>; templates, refs,
    signatures, magic words and comments dropped. Migration 002.

 -- Jeff Gardner <mailmasker-api01@forge.name>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:10:00 -0600

